, {"t_ms": 25029, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01AB6ECh5QXpKanLocyR2VSs", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 25029, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01AB6ECh5QXpKanLocyR2VSs", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 30180, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled payments back to its last healthy release and opened the SEV2. The error rate is back to normal.\n\n1. **Which service:** There's no service called `payments`. I tried a few likely names and found `payments-api`. It was running v5.1.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west, was marked unhealthy and had an 18% error rate. Its release history shows v5.1.0 as degraded and v5.0.0 as the most recent healthy production release.\n2. **Rollback:** I rolled `payments-api` back to v5.0.0, and the rollback finished in all three regions. A follow-up check shows the service healthy, with the error rate down to 0.2%.\n3. **Incident:** I opened INC-0001 (SEV2, `payments-api`), which paged on-call. It records the bad v5.1.0 deploy, the rollback to v5.0.0, and next steps: confirm error rates stay down and find what broke in v5.1.0.\n\nI found `payments-api` by guessing names and can't list every service, so if another payments service was deployed this morning I wouldn't have seen it. If one exists, give me its name and I'll check it too.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01Tue55nYkRMaV5fLGyutxyb", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01KB4Wz8oRJRYdMXCTpHm1qS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"